  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="work" n="189">
        <pb n="239"/>
        <head>Another on the same.</head>
        <head>189 — ii — IV. — <quote>My mouth shall speak wisdom</quote><ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a1" target="#n1" n="1"/>.</head>
        <div type="section">
          <ab n="1">When I consider what the river is of which <persName>David</persName> sings, whose currents or streams<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a2" target="#n2" n="2"/>, he says, gladden the church, which is the city of God, I look toward the tongue of the great <persName>John</persName> the high-priest, who rightly defines theology (<foreign xml:lang="grc">θεολογία</foreign>), and soars and is lifted up by means of doctrines<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a3" target="#n3" n="3"/>, and by means of the instruction contained in admonitions was<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a4" target="#n4" n="4"/> widely poured forth, and overwhelms like the sea, and in the matter of openly rebuking sin acts with boldness (<foreign xml:lang="grc">παρρησία</foreign>), and hastens<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a5" target="#n5" n="5"/> [to imitate the model and pattern of <persName>John</persName> the Baptist and Forerunner<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a6" target="#n6" n="6"/>, so as to choose and prefer beheading<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a7" target="#n7" n="7"/> rather than not to <pb n="240"/> speak and contend on behalf of the law of God. In his memory, <persName>Christ</persName>, God, establish the souls of us all, and deliver us according to the abundance of thy great mercy.</ab>
        </div>
      </div>
      <noteGrp>
        <note xml:id="n1" target="#a1" n="1"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 239, n. 2</orig></choice> Ps. xlix, 4.</note>
        <note xml:id="n2" target="#a2" n="2"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 239, n. 3</orig></choice> Id. xlvi, 5 (not quoted, and cited as xlvii).</note>
        <note xml:id="n3" target="#a3" n="3"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 239, n. 4</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>dogmas (<foreign xml:lang="grc">δόγματα</foreign>)</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n4" target="#a4" n="4"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 239, n. 5</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>is</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n5" target="#a5" n="5"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 239, n. 6</orig></choice> Matth. xiv, 3-5.</note>
        <note xml:id="n6" target="#a6" n="6"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 239, n. 7</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>after the pattern of the Forerunner and follows that model</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n7" target="#a7" n="7"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 239, n. 8</orig></choice> Ibid. 9-11 <quote>But because of the oaths and the guests..... to her mother</quote> (verbal diff.).</note>
      </noteGrp>
